- How would you adapt the system if two channels drop out permanently for several seconds?
- What diagnostics would you add to detect permutation drift across bins in real time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time, multi-source ICA with nonstationary acoustics and hardware constraints; requires concrete cadence, buffer sizes, latency budgeting, and evaluation methodology.

## Key Concepts
- Online convolutive ICA: frequency-domain approach with per-bin demixing matrices
- Joint diagonalization vs per-bin ICA: joint diagonalization enforces consistency across frequency bins
- Cross-bin permutation: magnitude envelope alignment, phase continuity, or reference-based correction
- Nonstationary tracking: online adaptation with forgetting factors
- Source-count robustness: detection via ICASSO, OR清水, or bayesian model order selection
- Latency budget: frame length, look-ahead, and processing time must sum to ≤20 ms
- Evaluation metrics: SIR, SAR, SDR (BSS_Eval), PESQ, STOI, and real-time CPU/memory profiling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Online ICA update with natural gradient
function onlineICA(X, W, lambda = 0.98, eps = 1e-8) {
  const [nMic, nFrame, nBin] = X.shape;
  const Xw = new Float32Array(nMic, nFrame, nBin);
  const W_new = new Float32Array(12, 3, nBin);

  for (let bin = 0; bin < nBin; bin++) {
    const X_bin = X.slice(:,:,bin);   // [nMic, nFrame]
    const W_bin = W[:,:,bin];          // [12, 3]

    // Whitening via exponential moving average
    const R = (1 - lambda) * X_bin @ X_bin.T + lambda * R;
    const V = inv(sqrtm(R + eps * eye(nMic)));
    const Xw_bin = V @ X_bin;

    // Natural gradient update: W ← W + μ(I - E[y y^T])W
    const Y = W_bin.T @ Xw_bin;               // [3, nFrame]
    const G = (Y @ Y.T) / nFrame;              // [3, 3]
    const delta = (eye(3) - G) @ W_bin;
    W_new[:,:,bin] = W_bin + 0.1 * delta;      // μ = 0.1
    Xw(:,:,bin) = Xw_bin;
  }
  return { W: W_new, Xw };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle a source-count mismatch (e.g., only 2 active speakers vs. 3 demixing channels)?
- What strategies would you use to detect and track moving speakers in real time?
- How does the choice of frame length affect the tradeoff between frequency resolution and latency?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design an online, adaptive BSS system in a mobile capture scenario with a moving platform and nonstationary noise. The new angle (drone stadium) exposes dynamic geometry, cross-bin permutation, and real-time constraints not covered by prior questions.

## Key Concepts

- Online whitening and adaptive estimation
- Joint diagonalization vs per-bin ICA
- Cross-bin permutation with temporal continuity
- Dynamic source-count handling on-device
- Practical evaluation: ground-truth sync, latency targets

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for online update
function update(Xframe) {
  W = onlineWhitening(Xframe);
  Y = jointDiagonalize(W*Xframe);
  return Y;
}
```

